1006-- **Decision (Apurva):** checking moves from repeated loops to rails and milestones, written centrally in `workflows/core/build-with-agents.md` (all projects) and applied here. (1) **Size the job:** small, mechanical fixes are done directly by the main thread with the one relevant check; terminal runs are for builds. (2) **Rules with no exceptions are tools:** a stylelint-based token check (`design-system/scripts/check_tokens.py`), run after every CSS edit by a Claude Code hook and at every commit by the git pre-commit gate. (3) **One review per run,** Codex against the spec, correctness only, style skipped; one fix pass; a second review only for blockers. (4) **Your eyes for looks:** one phone walkthrough per journey; your notes and review findings go on one list, fixed in one pass. (5) **Foundation check** before anything others build on: "who uses this next, and what will they need?" (6) **Every bug gets its smallest test.** (7) **Unattended chain:** `scripts/run-chain.sh` runs token pass → A1 → A2 → B, each in a fresh headless session with a turn cap, ending in `DONE` / `STOPPED` in `docs/runs/STATUS.md`; a main-thread scheduled check-in reviews each report and writes rulings to `docs/runs/RULINGS.md`. Set-up brief: `docs/renders/2026-11-09-rails/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md`.
1007-- **Why:** reviews checked work against its brief, so a wrong rule passed every time (D-99); slow checks ran on every change while fast ones didn't exist; reviewers asked to find problems always find something, which caused loops. Sources: Anthropic's Claude Code best practices (hooks for no-exception rules; review against the spec, skip style), Pawel Huryn (review results, not code; smallest test per bug; human eyes for taste), Gabor Meyer via Aakash Gupta (effort in the spec; reviews before building).
1008-- **Rejected:** a "can't finish until checks pass" Stop hook (several tabs share this folder, so one tab's half-done CSS would block another); a hand-written guard instead of stylelint; running the chain from a cloud scheduled task (it can't reach the Mac's Claude Code, Codex or Chrome).
