- **Should-fix — D-101 o04:** [app/core/auth.js:23](app/core/auth.js:23) checks the first digit before overlength. Consequently, `12345678901` and `56789012345` show “Mobile numbers start with…” instead of the required “That’s more than 10 digits. Check the number.” Neither has a +91 / 0 prefix. Prioritize overlength after cleaning and add this case to `tests/signin-d101.mjs`.

No other correctness findings in the scoped changes. Review was read-only; verified this case with the auth functions, without running the browser suites.
